The LGPL Python packages (python-telegram-bot, pystray, py7zr and its
dependencies) are distributed as unmodified, separately installed packages
under the bundled Python runtime (site-packages), so they can be replaced
by the user. Their complete license texts are in licenses/ and in each
package's .dist-info/licenses/ directory.

FFmpeg differs in shape: it is a native library inside the
opencv-python-headless wheel (under cv2/), not a separate package, so
replacing it means replacing that wheel. Its third-party notices ship at
cv2/LICENSE-3RD-PARTY.txt.
